    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Bienville Parish is a historically rich and naturally beautiful parish located in Northwest Louisiana, where pine forests, rolling hills, and quiet communities define the landscape.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://louisianalivingandbusiness.com/blogs/exploring-louisiana-s-64-parishes-from-largest-to-smallest/bienville-parish-louisiana"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Bienville Parish is the site of the 1934 Bonnie and Clyde ambush near Gibsland, a moment in American outlaw history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://louisianalivingandbusiness.com/blogs/exploring-louisiana-s-64-parishes-from-largest-to-smallest/bienville-parish-louisiana"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Bienville Parish hosts an annual Bonnie and Clyde Festival featuring vintage cars and Depression‑era storytelling.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://louisianalivingandbusiness.com/blogs/exploring-louisiana-s-64-parishes-from-largest-to-smallest/bienville-parish-louisiana"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Arcadia, the parish seat of Bienville Parish, is a historic town known for antique shops, restaurants, and its ties to Bonnie and Clyde.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
